  "question": {
    "text": "A mouse of mass \\(\\mathrm{m}\\) jumps on the outside edge of a rotating ceiling fan of moment of inertia I and radius \\(\\mathrm{R}\\). The fractional loss of angular velocity of the fan as a result is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0H4Ij",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{m R^2}{\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{mR}^2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iDOVZ",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{I}{I+m R^2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LwIlk",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{I}-\\mathrm{mR}^2}{\\mathrm{I}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WlyQr",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{I-m R^2}{I+m R^2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \\(I \\omega_0=\\left(\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{mR}^2\\right) \\omega\\)\n\\(\\omega_0 \\rightarrow\\) Initial angular velocity\n\\(\\omega=\\frac{I \\omega_0}{I+m R^2}\\)\n\\(\\omega \\rightarrow\\) Final angular velocity\nSo, \\(\\frac{\\omega_0-\\omega}{\\omega_0}=I-\\frac{I}{I+m R^2}=\\frac{m R^2}{I+m R^2}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
